From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:33:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Keep render work records in
 ASC-cached session slots by default

Each render's TA and FS work records are written at every publication
and read by the firmware while it prepares, starts and posts each
stage. In their per-VM work objects they are mapped uncached; macOS maps
its work records ASC-cached.

Make g16_render_work_pool default to 1 and g16_render_work_cached
default to 1. Every render then writes its work records into its unit's
slot in the ASC-cached session object, mapped for the hardware at a
context-0 lower address reserved at boot before any VM exists. Render
units are claimed device-wide and held until their render retires, so
no two renders in flight share a slot; the session objects are never
dropped, so no cached mapping is unmapped at client exit; and the
firmware cleans and invalidates each work record at its stage's post.
This is the same structure as the render microsequence slots, which are
already on by default.

g16_render_work_cached=0 at run time returns to the uncached copy, and
aurora.g16_render_work_pool=0 on the command line to each unit's own
work objects.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_core.rs | 4 ++--
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs | 8 ++++----
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_core.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_core.rs
index 56e2c57757..b93c69f634 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_core.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_core.rs
@@ -296,8 +296,8 @@ fn init(module: &'static kernel::ThisModule) -> impl PinInit<Self, Error> {
             description: "G16: 1 (default) = render microsequences in session slots per unit, uncached and ASC-cached copies; 0 = each unit's own sequence objects",
         },
         g16_render_work_pool: u32 {
-            default: 0,
-            description: "G16: 1 = render TA and FS work records in session slots per unit, uncached and ASC-cached copies",
+            default: 1,
+            description: "G16: 1 (default) = render TA and FS work records in session slots per unit, uncached and ASC-cached copies; 0 = each unit's own work objects",
         },
         g16_host_records: u32 {
             default: 0,
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
index cf79f5cd22..50303b5ff8 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
@@ -2949,7 +2949,7 @@ pub(crate) fn pb_slot(k: usize) -> usize {
     "G16: 1 = every render of a VM binds one PB manager and hardware-buffer id (slot 0, unit 0's heap), shared by its renders in flight; each keeps its own unit (default 0: one PB per unit; latched at the first render command, set it as a module option)"
 );
 
-/// `g16_render_work_pool` (load time, default 0). 1: at boot two session objects, one uncached
+/// `g16_render_work_pool` (load time, default 1). 1: at boot two session objects, one uncached
 /// and one ASC-cached, each hold one TA and one FS work record slot per render unit. The firmware
 /// maps them like the units' own work objects, and the hardware reads them at a context-0 lower
 /// address reserved at boot (graph::RENDER_WORK_LOWER). Every render then writes its work records
@@ -2962,8 +2962,8 @@ pub(crate) fn render_work_pool() -> bool {
     module_parameters::g16_render_work_pool.value() == 1
 }
 
-/// Storage of `g16_render_work_cached` (runtime 0644, default 0).
-static RENDER_WORK_CACHED: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(0);
+/// Storage of `g16_render_work_cached` (runtime 0644, default 1).
+static RENDER_WORK_CACHED: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(1);
 
 /// With `g16_render_work_pool`, whether renders published from now on use the ASC-cached copy of
 /// their unit's work slot (the class macOS gives its work records, GPU-MAP trip E) instead of the
@@ -2978,7 +2978,7 @@ pub(crate) fn render_work_cached() -> bool {
     RENDER_WORK_CACHED_PARM,
     RENDER_WORK_CACHED,
     "g16_render_work_cached",
-    "G16: with g16_render_work_pool=1, publish renders with the ASC-cached copy of their unit's work record slot (default 0: the uncached copy; runtime 0644)"
+    "G16: with g16_render_work_pool=1, publish renders with the ASC-cached copy of their unit's work record slot (default 1; 0: the uncached copy; runtime 0644)"
 );
 
 /// Storage of `g16_behind_initbm` (runtime 0644, default 1).
-- 
